.TH DL\-SENTINEL 1 "August 2026" "DL Sentinel 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dl\-sentinel \- scan a repository for secrets, vulnerable dependencies and insecure configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sentinel
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B DL Sentinel
scans a directory with six scanners \- secrets, dependencies, source code,
container and infrastructure configuration, API definitions and smart contracts
\- and reports structured findings.
.PP
Scanning is local and read\-only. Scanned code is never executed, source is
never uploaded, and secret values are redacted before they reach a finding, a
report or a log line. No network request is made unless a network\-backed
vulnerability data source is explicitly enabled in configuration.
.PP
The command is installed as both
.B dl\-sentinel
and
.BR sentinel .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI scan " [path]"
Scan a directory and print a report. Defaults to the current directory.
.TP
.BI baseline " [path]"
Record the current findings as a baseline file, so a later scan can report only
findings introduced afterwards.
.TP
.BI report " file"
Re\-render a saved JSON report in another format without re\-scanning.
.TP
.B rules
List every rule from every registered scanner.
.TP
.BI graph " [path]"
Render the deployment surface described by Compose, Kubernetes and Dockerfile
sources as JSON or Mermaid.
.TP
.B plugins
Load and describe external scanner plugins without scanning.
.TP
.B version
Print the tool name and version.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-format " format"
Output format: \fBterminal\fR (default), \fBjson\fR, \fBmarkdown\fR or \fBsarif\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-output " path"
Write the report to a file instead of standard output.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " path"
Use an explicit \fBsentinel.yml\fR instead of discovering one in the target.
.TP
.BI \-\-scanners " ids"
Run only a comma\-separated subset of scanners.
.TP
.BI \-\-fail\-on " severities"
Override the severities that cause a failed policy for this run.
.TP
.BI \-\-baseline " path"
Compare against a baseline and report only findings absent from it.
.TP
.BI \-\-write\-baseline " path"
Write a baseline of this scan's findings after reporting.
.TP
.B \-\-paths
Correlate findings into candidate attack paths and append them to the report.
.TP
.BI \-\-plugin " spec"
Load an external scanner plugin. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Suppress progress output on standard error.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI colour. Also honoured through the \fBNO_COLOR\fR environment variable.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Scan completed and the policy passed.
.TP
.B 1
Findings were present at a severity listed in \fBpolicy.failOn\fR.
.TP
.B 2
Scan or internal error.
.TP
.B 64
Usage error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B sentinel.yml
Per\-project configuration read from the scan target: include and exclude
globs, per\-scanner settings, suppression rules and the failure policy.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Scan the current directory:
.B sentinel scan .
.TP
Produce SARIF for a CI code\-scanning upload:
.B sentinel scan . \-\-format sarif \-\-output results.sarif
.TP
Adopt the scanner on an existing codebase, then fail only on new findings:
.B sentinel baseline . && sentinel scan . \-\-baseline .sentinel\-baseline.json
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation in
.IR /usr/share/doc/dlsentinel/ ,
and at
.IR https://github.com/Dhiva\-Labs/dl\-sentinel .
